    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "Tarnmoor is the first settled ground the road out of the port reaches, and the last one every load off the western moor passes through: the four villages beyond it all come down this way. What it sends out itself is farmed rather than worked \u2014 a flat-floored basin ringed by limestone, hay and grain for six months and a lake for the other six \u2014 with ore picked off the rubble at the foot of the tower standing in it, which comes up in daylight while everything else on this road comes up on a line."
  },
